{"type":"standard","title":"Matthew Dunlap","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Matthew Dunlap</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q6790437","titles":{"canonical":"Matthew_Dunlap","normalized":"Matthew Dunlap","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Matthew Dunlap</span></span>"},"pageid":15784952,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/70/Matt_Dunlap_%28cropped_headshot%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":279,"height":424},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/70/Matt_Dunlap_%28cropped_headshot%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":279,"height":424},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377459614","tid":"38e10d2f-bc0f-11f1-a632-e0ee9a96c7ec","timestamp":"2026-09-29T14:08:19Z","description":"American politician from Maine (born 1964)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthew_Dunlap","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthew_Dunlap?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthew_Dunlap?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Matthew_Dunlap"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthew_Dunlap","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Matthew_Dunlap","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthew_Dunlap?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Matthew_Dunlap"}},"extract":"Matthew Dunlap is an American politician from Maine who has served as the Maine state auditor since November 2022. He previously held the same position from January to October 2021. A member of the Democratic Party, Dunlap was secretary of state of Maine from January 7, 2013, to January 4, 2021, and previously from 2005 to 2011. In 2012, he sought to become his party's nominee to replace retiring Olympia Snowe, but lost in the primary to State Senator Cynthia Dill. He is currently the Democratic nominee for Maine's 2nd congressional district in the 2026 election, facing off against Paul LePage.","extract_html":"<p><b>Matthew Dunlap</b> is an American politician from Maine who has served as the Maine state auditor since November 2022. He previously held the same position from January to October 2021. A member of the Democratic Party, Dunlap was secretary of state of Maine from January 7, 2013, to January 4, 2021, and previously from 2005 to 2011. In 2012, he sought to become his party's nominee to replace retiring Olympia Snowe, but lost in the primary to State Senator Cynthia Dill. He is currently the Democratic nominee for Maine's 2nd congressional district in the 2026 election, facing off against Paul LePage.</p>"}